COPY public.complaints (id, description, created_at, user_id, pnr_number, status, entity_type, entity_id, image_url, resolution_description, resolution_image_url) FROM stdin;
2	Main electronic train arrival LED display board at Platform 1 entrance is flickering violently with scrambled text, misleading departing passengers on train schedules.	2026-03-12 18:16:52.946082	2	8492015632	Resolved	Station	SBC	/uploads/complaint_2_display_glitch.jpg	Signal & Telecom (S&T) engineering team rebooted and recalibrated the display controller, replacing the frayed interface ribbon cable. Live train feed restored.	/uploads/resolution_2_display_restored.jpg
3	Drinking water dispenser booth on Platform 2 is discharging muddy brownish water with an unpleasant odor. Passengers are unable to drink or refill bottles.	2026-03-27 00:13:22.724875	2	\N	Pending	Station	HAS	/uploads/complaint_3_water_tap.jpg	\N	\N
4	Wall-mounted electrical charging outlet in the passenger waiting lounge is physically cracked with exposed live wiring, posing a serious electric shock hazard.	2026-05-06 16:24:28.396471	2	\N	Resolved	Station	HLN	/uploads/complaint_4_broken_socket.jpg	Station electrical maintenance crew removed the damaged fixture and installed a brand new insulated 3-pin modular switchboard with earthing.	/uploads/resolution_4_socket_repaired.jpg
5	Reserved berths 45 and 46 in Coach C3 forcibly occupied by unauthorized unreserved passengers who refuse to clear and have obstructed the walkway with luggage.	2026-05-12 09:57:22.391442	3	2849103857	Resolved	Train	12028	/uploads/complaint_5_train_crowd.jpg	On-duty Traveling Ticket Examiner (TTE) accompanied by RPF personnel boarded at the next stop, verified PNR credentials, relocated unauthorized passengers, and restored seats.	/uploads/resolution_5_seats_restored.jpg
6	Coach B5 bio-toilet door latch is broken and will not lock from the interior, preventing passengers from using the restroom safely while the train is in motion.	2026-05-12 18:17:27.460363	3	6391048291	Pending	Train	22691	/uploads/complaint_6_toilet_lock.png	\N	\N
7	Severe waste overflow around dustbins at Platform 4 foot overbridge staircase with littered plastic waste, discarded food packets, and flies creating unhygienic conditions.	2026-06-18 09:52:07.121861	7	\N	Resolved	Station	YPR	/uploads/complaint_7_platform_waste.jpg	Station housekeeping task force mobilized under Swachh Rail drive. Entire area cleared, thoroughly pressure washed, sanitized, and new high-capacity bins placed.	/uploads/resolution_7_platform_cleaned.jpg
8	Booking clerk at PRS Ticket Counter #2 behaved discourteously, refused to accept standard digital UPI QR payment, and turned away waiting passengers.	2026-06-18 10:39:02.639476	8	\N	Pending	Station	ACH	/uploads/complaint_8_ticket_counter.jpg	\N	\N
1	Air conditioning in Coach B2 completely non-functional since departure. Compartment temperature has crossed 34 degrees Celsius with elderly passengers experiencing severe distress.	2026-03-12 18:04:05.419304	1	4521893214	Resolved	Train	12657	/uploads/complaint_1_ac_failure.jpg	Attended by on-board electrical maintenance technician at Katpadi Junction. Defective cooling relay replaced; coach temperature restored to 23 degrees Celsius.	/uploads/resolution_1_ac_restored.jpg
\.
